Actually, you lose more than one turn; you lose the turn you drop the
bag, plus any additional turns the "normal" speed monsters get
against you during that time.  You also chain yourself to that location,
because you can't abandon your bag and run effectively; and you can't
pick the bag back up again without being Burdened.

You also lose potential ranged-attack turns when things appear round a
corner at a distance -- and you open yourself up for the dangerous
"double attack" that monsters occasionally get if they're faster than
you.  For example:

I wanted to make locusts faster than an average player, but the speed
system kept giving them dual attacks when I did, so I had to tone them
back some.  This is likely why the Riders are only speed 12 ("normal"
speed) as well, so that only a player who has penalized themselves in
some way will get hit twice in one turn with, say, a sickness attack.

