It isn't solely the solvability rate; it's that huge portions of the
game that were clearly intended to be a challenge are totally
bypassable with only trivial effort.  "Gehennom is boring" is an 
excellent example of this, as most players find it boring even on their
first time through.

Demon bribery is another excellent example in two ways: first, if you
don't bribe the demons, it doesn't matter since they can't do anything
to hurt a player who's strong enough to make it to them in the first
place.  Second, the "bribe" they'll take can be insignificantly small (I
carry 10GP in open, they'll always ask for less), rendering the other
half of the "challenge" meaningless.  With both halves of the "demon
prince lair" problem bypassable, this leaves that part of the game
broken.  There are many other examples of this.

